  <h1>No Loading Bars, No Waiting: Why kodinitools.com Is Built for Maximum Speed</h1>

  <div class="blog-meta">
    <span class="blog-meta-badge">Performance</span>
    <span>September 27, 2026</span>
    <span>· 4 min read</span>
  </div>

  <p>
    If you want to quickly edit an image, trim an audio file or convert a document online, you want one thing above all: to get started right away. Nobody wants to sit through endless loading times, struggle with sign-up forms or click away ad banners.
  </p>

  <p>
    That is why kodinitools.com is built from the ground up so that its tools are ready to use directly in your browser – no detours, no data stored on third-party servers and, above all, lightning fast.
  </p>

  <p>
    A recent test with Google PageSpeed Insights shows what this means for your everyday work in front of the screen – and how much a series of targeted optimisations achieved within a single day.
  </p>

  <h2>A Perfect Score: 100 out of 100 on Desktop</h2>

  <p>
    When you open kodinitools.com on your laptop or PC, there is no noticeable delay. Google awards the top score:
  </p>

  <figure class="blog-demo">
    <img
      src="/image/speed-desktop-blog-en.webp"
      alt="Google PageSpeed Insights, desktop view: kodinitools.com scores 100 for performance, 94 for accessibility, 92 for best practices and 100 for SEO; First Contentful Paint 0.3 s, Largest Contentful Paint 0.6 s, Total Blocking Time 0 ms, Cumulative Layout Shift 0"
      width="1920"
      height="945"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <figcaption>PageSpeed Insights on desktop: 100 out of 100 points for performance.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Ready in 0.3 seconds:</strong> In the blink of an eye, the first content is visible to you (First Contentful Paint).</li>
    <li><strong>Fully loaded in 0.6 seconds:</strong> Even the largest element in the visible area is in place in well under a second (Largest Contentful Paint).</li>
    <li><strong>No stuttering, no freezing:</strong> Script blocking time is 0 milliseconds (Total Blocking Time) – the page responds to every click without delay.</li>
    <li><strong>Nothing jumps:</strong> With a layout shift score of 0 (CLS), every element stays exactly where it belongs.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Data from real visitors in the Chrome UX Report confirms it too: the Core Web Vitals assessment for desktop is passed.
  </p>

  <h2>Strong on the Go, Too: 97 out of 100 on Your Smartphone</h2>

  <p>
    On mobile devices, connections on the go are often unreliable and smartphones have less computing power than a desktop computer. That is why Google simulates an average smartphone with a throttled mobile connection in its test. Even so, the mobile version scores 97 points:
  </p>

  <figure class="blog-demo">
    <img
      src="/image/speed-mobile-blog-en.webp"
      alt="Google PageSpeed Insights, mobile view: kodinitools.com scores 97 for performance, 94 for accessibility, 92 for best practices and 100 for SEO"
      width="1920"
      height="945"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <figcaption>PageSpeed Insights on mobile: 97 points for performance, 100 points for SEO.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Something to see right away:</strong> The first content appears after 1.4 seconds, and the visible area is also built up after 1.4 seconds (First Contentful Paint, Speed Index).</li>
    <li><strong>Inputs respond instantly:</strong> Script blocking time is a negligible 10 milliseconds (Total Blocking Time). When you tap a button, the interface reacts immediately.</li>
    <li><strong>Stable layout, no mis-taps:</strong> Many mobile pages jump around while loading, so you accidentally tap the wrong thing. On our pages the layout shift is 0 (CLS).</li>
    <li><strong>Technically clean:</strong> A full 100 points for SEO, 94 points for accessibility and 92 points for best practices.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>From 89 to 97 Points: Before and After</h2>

  <p>
    In the first test that morning, mobile performance was still at 89 points. After a series of targeted optimisations, the comparison looks like this:
  </p>

  <div class="blog-table-wrap">
    <table class="blog-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Metric (smartphone)</th>
          <th>First test</th>
          <th>Now</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Performance</td><td>89 points</td><td><strong>97 points</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Largest Contentful Paint</td><td>3.6 s</td><td><strong>2.6 s</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Speed Index</td><td>3.0 s</td><td><strong>1.4 s</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Total Blocking Time</td><td>30 ms</td><td><strong>10 ms</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cumulative Layout Shift</td><td>0.015</td><td><strong>0</strong></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    On desktop, the score went from 97 to a full 100 points, and the Largest Contentful Paint dropped from 0.8 to 0.6 seconds.
  </p>

  <h2>What We Optimised</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Leaner images:</strong> The large header image now uses the modern WebP format. The logo and Swiss flag in the navigation were resized to the size they are actually displayed at – the logo alone shrank from around 150 KB to 2 KB.</li>
    <li><strong>First things first:</strong> The browser loads the header image with top priority, before less important elements get their turn.</li>
    <li><strong>No jumping while loading:</strong> The header image and headline reserve their space from the start, so nothing slides down when content loads in.</li>
    <li><strong>Notices without delay:</strong> The cookie notice appears with the very first render instead of popping in afterwards.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What Comes Next</h2>

  <p>
    At 2.6 seconds, the Largest Contentful Paint on smartphones is now only just above the 2.5-second mark at which Google rates the value as "good". That last tenth of a second is our next target, so the mobile tools feel just as weightless as they do on desktop.
  </p>

  <div class="tip-box">
    <p><strong>Our benchmark:</strong> Simple operation, respect for your time and reliable tools – that remains the benchmark for kodinitools.com.</p>
  </div>

